AGENT CONTRACT
Each agent declares:
purpose
input schema
output schema
tool allowlist
data scope
tenant scope
budget
timeout
retry policy
risk level

COORDINATION
Use typed events/tasks rather than free-form agent-to-agent side effects.
Support parent/child runs and deterministic checkpoints.

MEMORY
Separate:
working memory
campaign memory
brand memory
performance memory
operational memory
Never treat unverified LLM-generated text as durable truth.

TASK DELEGATION
Coordinator may delegate bounded tasks only after policy evaluation.
No recursive unbounded agent creation.

AUTONOMOUS BUSINESS LOOPS
Daily:
sync → rank → recommend → draft → approve/publish → reconcile → analyze → optimize.
Event-driven:
promotion starts, price changes, conversion spikes, provider failures, campaign fatigue, security events.

SELF-HEALING
IncidentAgent may diagnose failures and propose remediation.
Automatic remediation allowed only for low-risk pre-approved actions such as:
retry transient job
restart failed worker
pause provider workflow
refresh safe caches
reconcile status
Never auto-modify credentials, financial data, or security policy without approval.

ESCALATION
Severity-based:
INFO → log
LOW → auto-remediate if safe
MEDIUM → operator review
HIGH → pause affected scope + escalate
CRITICAL → activate kill switch + incident workflow

BUSINESS CONTROL PLANE
Mission Control must expose:
active agents
current tasks
blocked tasks
pending approvals
budgets
autonomy mode
kill switches
recent decisions
recovery actions
incidents
decision explanations

FIRST BOUNDED IMPLEMENTATION
Inspect current automation/agent code.
Define typed agent contracts, tool permissions, budgets, checkpoints, audit events, and coordinator interface.
Add tests for permission denial, tenant isolation, budget enforcement, recursive delegation prevention, and kill-switch behavior.
Update architecture, security, checklist, exec planning.
STOP after one bounded slice.

DEFINITION OF DONE
Agent autonomy is complete only when permissions, budget, policy, checkpoints, auditability, failure handling, and safe shutdown are verified.
